# Zone 1, room 5: Wall-kick climb. Phase 1 grey box.
# BUILD.md s5 tech 5: "climb a single wall with neutral kicks. Taught by a well"; s5 Wall-kick
# "900 u/s up, 240 u/s away ... Lets the player climb a single wall"; s15 Movement: "Wall-kick
# climbs a single wall without the player ever feeling stuck to it".
#
# Layout. The corridor from the west door opens into a well 384 u (12 tiles) wide whose one
# clingable surface is its east wall (its face at x 704); every other wall is smooth. The wall's top
# is the exit floor, 2176 u (68 tiles) above the well's floor, and the corridor beyond leads to the
# east door. The room is 36 tiles wide: a well is tall, not wide, and the camera centres a room
# narrower than the view.
#
# Stand-ins: none needed (a wall is a wall).
#
# How it teaches. The jump at the wall clings at its top; from there a kick on each cling climbs
# 175.6 u every 24 ticks, never stuck to the wall (each cling is left the tick after it starts). The
# first kicks are over the well's floor, where a fall is safe; the whole height is twelve kicks.
#
# Why up the wall (every number measured: docs/feel_log/2026-10-19-zone1-b.md). Away from the wall
# the strongest climb is the floor's jump, air jump and up-dash (554 u), the Ember Toss thrown from
# their top, a fall to the floor that gives everything back and the teleport 400 u up, then the air
# jump and up-dash again: 1313 u. Using the wall without a kick or a wall-jump (the first
# cling since the floor gives back the air jump and dash, an up-dash straight from the cling, the
# toss's landing trick, and a second fresh cling) tops out 2048 u up, 128 u short of the exit floor
# (tests/replay/zone1/05_control_no_kick, one toss). Kicks are not the only way up the wall, and
# the room does not try to make them so (docs/adr/0016): a wall-jump gives back the air dash
# (BUILD.md's wall-jump row: "Resets double jump and air dash"), so a wall-jump and an up-dash on
# the next tick, from every cling, climbs the same wall at 10.5 u a tick against the kicks' 7.3
# (tests/replay/zone1/05_wall_jump_dash_cycle: over the top 85 ticks sooner). That is tech 6's
# rhythm, taught in the next room, and it needs a player who has put wall-jump and dash together
# already. Kicks are the plain way: one button on a steady rhythm, nothing spent, the stick held
# toward the wall the whole climb, which is what the room's first twelve clings teach.
room zone1/05_wall_kick_climb
size 36 78
spawn 74 2400
